.TH GANDER 1 "November 2026" "gander 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gander \- preview a local git repository, offline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gander
.RI [ options ]
.I path
.br
.B gander
.RI [ options ]
.I name
.br
.B gander
.B current
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B gander
.RB [ \-h | \-V ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gander
serves a small web UI for a local git repository on
.B 127.0.0.1
and opens it in your browser: a file tree on the left, live previews on the
right. Markdown, images, animated GIFs, video, PDFs and source code are all
rendered locally, and the view refreshes as the repository changes.
.PP
Everything is local. There is no network code, no CDN and no telemetry; the
bundled UI is the only thing served. The previewed directory must be a git
repository \(em a
.I .git
directory, or a
.I .git
file for a linked worktree. Given a plain directory,
.B gander
prints a line and exits without starting a server.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I path
Preview the git repository at
.IR path .
.TP
.I name
Preview a repository named in the config file's
.B [paths]
section. Names are matched case-insensitively and a leading
.B ~
expands to
.BR $HOME .
A directory that exists on disk wins over a shortcut of the same name.
.TP
.B current
Preview the current working directory (same as
.BR . ).
.TP
.B gander
With no target, print the command list and exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-port " " \fIn\fR
Listen on port
.IR n .
The default,
.BR 0 ,
picks a free port.
.TP
.B \-\-host " " \fIaddr\fR
Bind to
.IR addr .
The default is
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.B \-\-web-root " " \fIdir\fR
Serve the UI assets from
.IR dir .
.TP
.B \-\-token " " \fIstr\fR
Require
.I str
to open the UI. The token is accepted as a
.B ?token=
query parameter (which sets a cookie) or as the
.B gander_token
cookie.
.TP
.B \-\-config " " \fIfile\fR
Read settings from
.I file
instead of the default location.
.TP
.B \-\-no-open
Do not launch a browser or app window.
.TP
.B \-\-app
Open the UI in a chromeless window instead of a browser tab. A
Chromium-family browser
.RB ( chromium ,
.BR google-chrome ,
.BR brave ,
.BR helium ,
.BR microsoft-edge ,
.BR vivaldi ,
and friends) is launched with
.B \-\-app=
and a throwaway profile under the cache directory, so your normal browser data
is never touched. If no such browser is found,
.B gander
says so and opens a normal tab instead. Firefox has no equivalent.
.TP
.B \-\-webview
Show the UI in an embedded window instead of a browser. This is experimental and
only present in a build made with
.BR "make WEBVIEW=1" .
That build prefers WebKitGTK (GTK3) and falls back to Qt Web Engine when GTK is
not present; force one with
.B "make WEBVIEW=gtk"
or
.BR "make WEBVIEW=qt" .
A build without a webview prints a note and opens a browser instead. The window
uses the bundled gander logo as its icon. Closing the embedded window stops the
server.
.TP
.B \-\-watch " " \fImode\fR
What live reload reacts to. One of
.BR commit " (the default: a commit, tag, branch switch or fetch),"
.BR all " (every file change) or"
.BR off .
Live reload uses
.B inotify
on Linux and a portable scan-and-diff elsewhere, so it works wherever gander
builds.
.TP
.B \-\-no-watch
Disable live reload (same as
.BR "\-\-watch off" ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the command list and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version (with the ASCII goose) and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from the first of these that exists:
.BR $GANDER_CONFIG ,
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gander/config ,
then
.BR $HOME/.config/gander/config .
A missing file is fine; every key has a built-in default. Command-line options
always win over the file.
.PP
The file is plain
.I key = value
lines; blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
or
.B ;
are ignored, and a value may be quoted. Recognised keys:
.TP
.B port
Integer; the port to listen on
.RB ( 0
picks a free one).
.TP
.B host
The interface to bind (default
.BR 127.0.0.1 ).
.TP
.B open
.B true
or
.BR false ;
whether to launch a browser on start (default
.BR true ).
.TP
.B app
.B true
or
.BR false ;
open a chromeless app window (default
.BR false ).
.TP
.B webview
.B true
or
.BR false ;
use the embedded webview (default
.BR false ;
see
.BR \-\-webview ).
.TP
.B watch
.BR commit ", " all " or " off .
.TP
.B web-root
Where the UI assets live.
.TP
.B token
Require this token to open the UI.
.TP
.B style
A stylesheet to layer over the bundled theme.
.PP
A stylesheet named
.I style.css
next to the config file is used automatically as the
.B style
value.
.SS Named paths
The
.B [paths]
section maps a short name to a repository, so
.B gander Nexus
opens it from anywhere:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
[paths]
Nexus = ~/Projects/Nexus
.EE
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GANDER_CONFIG
The config file to read, unless
.B \-\-config
is given.
.TP
.B GANDER_WEB
The directory holding the UI assets, used when
.B \-\-web-root
is not given.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base for the default config location.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base for the throwaway profile used by
.BR \-\-app .
.TP
.B HOME
Base for the default config location and the
.B \-\-app
profile.
.TP
.B PATH
Searched for the browser launched by
.BR \-\-app .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including
.B \-\-help
and
.BR \-\-version ).
.TP
.B 1
The target is missing, is not a directory, or is not a git repository; or the
server could not start.
.TP
.B 2
An unknown option was given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/gander/config
The default configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gander/style.css
A user stylesheet layered over the bundled theme.
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview the repository in the current directory:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
gander current
.EE
.RE
.PP
Preview a named repository in a chromeless window on a fixed port:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
gander Nexus --app --port 8080
.EE
.RE
.PP
Serve for a shared machine, gated by a token:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
gander ~/work/api --host 127.0.0.1 --token hunter2
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1)
.PP
The bundled UI offers full-text search over the working tree (press
.BR / ).
